process-gpu-messages.m's process kinds spawned on the machine's GPU
(docs/INPROGRESS.md, GPU processes without omp target, step 4e): a counter
that takes add(N) and get(Reply), two processes that play ping-pong through
the host's mailboxes, and a summer that takes a list and a string. A closure
in a message cannot cross to the GPU, which the host finds when it copies the
message for the GPU, and the program ends.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-gpu-messages.m -o %t2
RUN: %libomp-env timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu | FileCheck %S/process-gpu-messages.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: merkc -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-gpu-messages.m -o %t
RUN: %libomp-env timeout -k 1 60 %t gpu | FileCheck %S/process-gpu-messages.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: not %libomp-env timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu closure 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CLOSURE --match-full-lines
CLOSURE:Mercury runtime: cannot copy a closure between the host and a GPU

Two hundred GPU processes that each take one message of two and end leave
none of the host's copies of their messages, nor any of the messages, nor
their arenas or their mailboxes' rings, though no target region ends.
RUN: %libomp-env MERK_CHECK_PINNED=1 MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu many 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MANY --match-full-lines
MANY:20300
MANY-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of host memory for devices' messages are allocated
MANY-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 messages are neither read nor freed
MANY-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated
